<title>USA: American Eagle to announce fleet plan.</title>
<headline>American Eagle to announce fleet plan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMR Corp's American Eagle regional airline said it will hold a media briefing Tuesday to discuss &quot;fleet planning decisions regarding regional jets.&quot;</p>
<p>The press briefing, held at AMR Corp's Fort Worth, Texas, headquarters, will start at 1030 EDT/1430 GMT.</p>
<p>American Eagle representatives did not provide additional details.</p>
<p>American Eagle is expected to announce an order for about 67 planes, either from Bombardier Inc's Canadair or from Brazil's state-owned Embraer SA, or from both, industry analysts said. The potential aircraft order is valued at more than $1 billion.</p>
</text>
